solution_md:
Or

<details><summary>Alcumus solution</summary>Let the centers of the circles be  $O_1$ ,  $O_2$ , and  $O_3$ . Let  $A$ ,  $B$ , and  $C$  be the vertices of the large equilateral triangle, and let  $T$  and  $U$  be the points of tangency, as shown.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, T, U;
pair[] O;

O[1] = dir(90);
O[2] = dir(90 + 120);
O[3] = dir(90 + 240);
A = (1 + sqrt(3))*dir(90);
B = (1 + sqrt(3))*dir(90 + 120);
C = (1 + sqrt(3))*dir(90 + 240);
T = O[1] + sqrt(3)/2*dir(30);
U = O[3] + sqrt(3)/2*dir(30);

draw(Circle(O[1],sqrt(3)/2));
draw(Circle(O[2],sqrt(3)/2));
draw(Circle(O[3],sqrt(3)/2));
draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--O[1]--O[3]--C);
draw(O[1]--T);
draw(O[3]--U);
draw(O[1]--O[2]--O[3]);

dot(" $O_1$ ", O[1], W);
dot(" $O_2$ ", O[2], SW);
dot(" $O_3$ ", O[3], S);
label(" $A$ ", A, N);
label(" $B$ ", B, SW);
label(" $C$ ", C, SE);
label(" $T$ ", T, NE);
label(" $U$ ", U, NE);
[/asy]

We see that triangle  $O_1 O_2 O_3$  is equilateral, with side length  $2 \cdot 3 = 6$ . Since  $\overline{AC}$  is tangent to the circles at  $T$  and  $U$ ,  $\angle O_1 TU = \angle O_3 UT = 90^\circ$ . Hence, quadrilateral  $O_1 TUO_3$  is a rectangle. Therefore,  $\overline{TU}$  is parallel to  $\overline{O_1 O_3}$ , which means that  $\overline{AC}$  is parallel to  $\overline{O_1 O_3}$ .

By symmetry,  $\overline{AO_1}$  bisects  $\angle BAC$ , so  $\angle O_1 AT = \angle BAC/2 = 60^\circ/2 = 30^\circ$ . Hence, triangle  $AO_1 T$  is  $30^\circ$ - $60^\circ$ - $90^\circ$ . Then  $AT = O_1 T \sqrt{3} = 3 \sqrt{3}$ . Similarly,  $UC = 3 \sqrt{3}$ . Also,  $TU = O_1 O_2 = 6$ . Therefore,
\[AC = AT + TU + UC = 3 \sqrt{3} + 6 + 3 \sqrt{3} = 6 \sqrt{3} + 6.\]Then the perimeter of triangle  $ABC$  is  $3 \cdot AC = \boxed{18 \sqrt{3} + 18}$ .</details>

