We work backwards:
\[
\begin{array}{c|ccccccccccccc}
k & n & n-1 & \tfrac{n-1}{16} & \tfrac{n-17}{16} & \tfrac{n-17}{32} & \tfrac{n-49}{32} & \tfrac{n-49}{64} & \tfrac{n-113}{64} & \tfrac{n-113}{256} & \tfrac{n-369}{256} & \tfrac{n-369}{512} & 3  
\hline
a_k & \tfrac{19}{87} & \tfrac{87}{19} & \tfrac{11}{19} & \tfrac{19}{11} & \tfrac{8}{11} & \tfrac{11}{8} & \tfrac{3}{8} & \tfrac{8}{3} & \tfrac{2}{3} & \tfrac{3}{2} & \tfrac{1}{2} & \tfrac{1}{2}
\end{array}
\]
Thus, we must have  $\frac{n-369}{512}=3 \implies n=1905,$  so the answer is  $1+9+0+5=\boxed{\textbf{(A)}\ 15}. \ \blacksquare$

