Trivially, the condition is equivalent to  $2^{|A|}+2^{|B|}+2^{|C|}=2^{|A \cup B\cup C|}$  which becomes   $$ 2^{100}+2^{100}+2^{|C|}=2^{|A \cup B\cup C|} $$     $$ 2^{101}+2^{|C|}=2^{|A \cup B\cup C|}. $$   Note that the unique positive integer solution to this is  $|C|=101$  and  $|A \cup B\cup C|=102,$  which we can see by converting to binary. We use the following diagram, where letters in intersections represent the number of elements in that intersection and outside the other parts of the diagram.
[asy]
/* Diagram credits to m5s*/
size(200);
defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
for(int i=0;i<=2;i=i+1)
draw(circle(dir(270+120*i),1.75));

