This is 2017 AMC 12 #17

<details><summary>Solution</summary>Listing out some numbers,
\begin{align*}
f(1) &= 1 
f(2) &= 1 \cdot f(1) = 1 
f(4)&= 2 \cdot f(2) = 2 =2^1
f(8) &= 4 \cdot f(4)=8=2^3 
f(16) &= 8 \cdot f(8)=64=2^6 
f(32)&=16 \cdot f(8)=2^{10} 
f(64) &=32 \cdot f(16)=2^{15} 
f(128)&=64 \cdot f(64)=2^{21} 
& \vdots
\end{align*}
From here, we can easily see that  $$ f(2^n)=2^{\frac{n(n-1)}{2}} \implies f(2^100)=2^{99 \cdot 50}=\boxed{2^{4950}} $$</details>

