[/asy] $P_A$  rotates  $P$  at angle of  $60$  degrees about  $A$ .
Do the same for  $P_B$  and  $P_C$ .

So we get the following. $AP = PP_A = P_AA = 1$  $BP = PP_B = P_BB = \sqrt{3}$  $CP = PP_C = P_CC = 2$ And we get the following triangle $\triangle AP_BP \equiv \triangle BP_CP \equiv \triangle CP_AP$  is right triangle with side length  $1, \sqrt{3}, 2$ . $\triangle APP_A$  is equilateral triangle with side length  $1$ . $\triangle BPP_B$  is equilateral triangle with side length  $\sqrt{3}$ . $\triangle CPP_C$  is equilateral triangle with side length  $2$ .

Therefore area of hexagon  $AP_BBP_CCP_A$  is
\[3 \times \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}(1+3+4) = \frac{7\sqrt{3}}{2} = 2 \triangle ABC\]

So area of  $\triangle ABC$  is  $\frac{7\sqrt{3}}{4}$ .
Thus  $\triangle ABC$  of side length is  $\boxed{\sqrt{7}}$ .

